slug] — the page routes keep the segment), { routing: \"prefix-except-default\" } when the default language is at the root and the others under /ru/…, /de/… (without `param` Mapled puts the language before the page). Mapled builds each language's address of a record from it (the editor's routes, Preview); a translated slug is the address in that language, a missing translation falls back. Leave it out on a site with one address for every language. The answer's manifest.integrationHash is the hash of the schema and these bindings — what the site is synced with from now on; check_integration reports inSync against it. Needs the builder plan.",
